{
  "$comment": [
    "Single source of truth for the Panda Code design system ('Graphite & Brass').",
    "Consumed by scripts/generate.mjs, which emits:",
    "  - apps/desktop/src/renderer/src/tokens.css   (CSS custom properties)",
    "  - apps/mobile/lib/theme/panda_tokens.dart    (Dart ThemeExtension)",
    "",
    "Colour value syntax:",
    "  '#rrggbb'      literal",
    "  '$name'        reference into `primitives`",
    "  '$name/NN'     that primitive at NN% alpha (NN may be fractional, e.g. 2.8)",
    "  'transparent'  fully transparent",
    "",
    "Design rules this file encodes:",
    "  - ONE accent, and it is brass. Blue is informational only, never 'selected'.",
    "  - Five-step surface ladder + `overlay` for floating surfaces. Nothing else.",
    "  - Status colours are semantic only: run/warn/danger/info.",
    "  - Mobile is the same scale as desktop with radii +2px and taller controls."
  ],

  "primitives": {
    "brass": "#d0a85d",
    "$comment_brassDeep": "Filled-button background. Mockups used #a97f2e, but near-white label text on it scores only 3.39:1 — button labels are ~10.5pt, so AA 4.5:1 applies, not AA-large. Darkened to the minimum that passes; see contrast.test.mjs.",
    "brassDeep": "#8f6b27",
    "$comment_brassDark": "Light-mode accent. Must NOT be the raw brass: #d0a85d on white is ~2.1:1. This value is the minimum darkening that clears AA on the DARKEST light surface it appears on (`panelStrong`, #e8eaee) — that is the contrast floor, not `panel`.",
    "brassDark": "#846520",
    "green": "#66c98b",
    "greenDeep": "#2f6948",
    "greenDark": "#1d7a4c",
    "amber": "#dfb45f",
    "amberDeep": "#6a5426",
    "amberDark": "#95650b",
    "red": "#ef6a7a",
    "redDeep": "#753641",
    "redDark": "#b03040",
    "blue": "#7ab7ff",
    "blueDeep": "#2a5480",
    "blueDark": "#1f66b8",
    "$comment_violet": "Entity identity, NOT a status: nested subagent cards and the Codex provider tag. It is exempt from the one-accent rule because it labels *what a thing is*, never whether it is selected — so it can never be confused with the brass selection state.",
    "violet": "#b78bff",
    "violetDeep": "#4c3475",
    "violetDark": "#63409f",
    "scrollGrey": "#8c97a6",
    "scrollGreyHi": "#a6b3c2",
    "scrollGreyLight": "#5a6473",
    "white": "#ffffff",
    "black": "#000000",
    "shadowDark": "#04060a",
    "shadowLight": "#10141c"
  },

  "themes": {
    "dark": {
      "surface": {
        "appBg": "#121315",
        "sidebar": "#17181b",
        "panelSoft": "#181a1e",
        "panel": "#1b1d21",
        "panelStrong": "#23262b",
        "panelHover": "#22252a",
        "$comment_hoverWash": "The translucent counterpart to `panelHover`, for controls that have no background of their own (ghost rows, toolbar icons, list items) and so must tint whatever rung they happen to sit on. Two steps only: `hoverWash` for a row, `hoverWashStrong` for a small target that needs to read as pressed. Before these existed, styles.css carried ten different white alphas doing this job by eye.",
        "hoverWash": "$white/6",
        "hoverWashStrong": "$white/10",
        "$comment_scrim": "The one dim behind a modal. Every dialog backdrop in the app used to pick its own near-black at its own alpha (0.4 / 0.5 / 0.52 / 0.78), so two overlays opened side by side dimmed the app by different amounts.",
        "scrim": "$shadowDark/62",
        "overlay": "#1e2126",
        "inputBg": "#11151d"
      },
      "line": {
        "lineSoft": "#262a31",
        "line": "#30343b",
        "lineHi": "#3d434c"
      },
      "text": {
        "text": "#f0f2f4",
        "muted": "#a3abb6",
        "subtle": "#727b88",
        "placeholder": "#5d6672"
      },
      "accent": {
        "solid": "$brassDeep",
        "on": "#fff6e2",
        "text": "$brass",
        "textHi": "#e7c98c",
        "edge": "$brass/34",
        "edgeStrong": "$brass/62",
        "wash": "$brass/13",
        "washStrong": "$brass/26"
      },
      "status": {
        "run": {
          "solid": "$greenDeep",
          "on": "#eafff2",
          "text": "$green",
          "edge": "$green/28",
          "wash": "$green/13"
        },
        "warn": {
          "solid": "$amberDeep",
          "on": "#f5e4bd",
          "text": "$amber",
          "edge": "$amber/28",
          "wash": "$amber/12"
        },
        "danger": {
          "solid": "$redDeep",
          "on": "#ffe4e8",
          "text": "$red",
          "edge": "$red/28",
          "wash": "$red/12"
        },
        "info": {
          "solid": "$blueDeep",
          "on": "#eaf3ff",
          "text": "$blue",
          "edge": "$blue/30",
          "wash": "$blue/13"
        },
        "$comment_agent": "Entity identity (subagent cards, Codex provider tag) — see `violet` in primitives. Shaped like a status so it flows through the same codegen, but it is not one.",
        "agent": {
          "solid": "$violetDeep",
          "on": "#f3ecff",
          "text": "$violet",
          "edge": "$violet/30",
          "wash": "$violet/12"
        }
      },
      "focus": { "ring": "$brass/24" },
      "scroll": {
        "thumb": "$scrollGrey/34",
        "thumbHover": "$scrollGreyHi/52",
        "track": "transparent"
      },
      "effects": {
        "panelSheen": {
          "type": "linearGradient",
          "angle": 180,
          "stops": [["$white/2.8", "0%"], ["transparent", "42%"]]
        },
        "overlaySheen": {
          "type": "linearGradient",
          "angle": 180,
          "stops": [["#23262b", "0%"], ["#1c1f24", "100%"]]
        },
        "elevCard": {
          "type": "shadow",
          "layers": [
            { "inset": true, "x": 0, "y": 1, "blur": 0, "spread": 0, "color": "$white/3.5" }
          ]
        },
        "elevButton": {
          "type": "shadow",
          "layers": [
            { "inset": true, "x": 0, "y": 1, "blur": 0, "spread": 0, "color": "$white/7" }
          ]
        },
        "elevPopover": {
          "type": "shadow",
          "layers": [
            { "inset": false, "x": 0, "y": 20, "blur": 48, "spread": 0, "color": "$shadowDark/56" },
            { "inset": true, "x": 0, "y": 1, "blur": 0, "spread": 0, "color": "$white/4" }
          ]
        }
      }
    },

    "light": {
      "$comment": [
        "Mobile-only for now — the desktop renderer is dark-only (`color-scheme: dark`).",
        "The ladder INVERTS rather than flattens: cards go white on grey so elevation still",
        "reads. Brass is the one value that cannot carry over literally: #d0a85d on white is",
        "~2.1:1 and fails AA, so text/edges use $brassDark while washes keep the original hue."
      ],
      "surface": {
        "appBg": "#f4f5f7",
        "sidebar": "#eceef1",
        "panelSoft": "#f8f9fa",
        "panel": "#ffffff",
        "panelStrong": "#e8eaee",
        "panelHover": "#eceef1",
        "$comment_hoverWash": "Inverts with the ladder: a white wash is invisible on a light surface, so light mode tints downward instead.",
        "hoverWash": "$black/5",
        "hoverWashStrong": "$black/9",
        "scrim": "$shadowLight/32",
        "overlay": "#ffffff",
        "inputBg": "#ffffff"
      },
      "line": {
        "lineSoft": "#e6e8ec",
        "line": "#d9dce1",
        "lineHi": "#c3c8d0"
      },
      "text": {
        "text": "#16181c",
        "muted": "#5b636e",
        "subtle": "#7f8792",
        "placeholder": "#8e95a0"
      },
      "accent": {
        "solid": "$brassDark",
        "on": "#fffaf0",
        "text": "$brassDark",
        "textHi": "#6d5316",
        "edge": "$brassDark/30",
        "edgeStrong": "$brassDark/55",
        "wash": "$brass/16",
        "washStrong": "$brass/30"
      },
      "status": {
        "run": {
          "solid": "#226b45",
          "on": "#f2fff8",
          "text": "$greenDark",
          "edge": "$greenDark/28",
          "wash": "$greenDark/10"
        },
        "warn": {
          "solid": "#7c5410",
          "on": "#fffaf0",
          "text": "$amberDark",
          "edge": "$amberDark/28",
          "wash": "$amber/18"
        },
        "danger": {
          "solid": "#a3313f",
          "on": "#fff3f4",
          "text": "$redDark",
          "edge": "$redDark/26",
          "wash": "$redDark/9"
        },
        "info": {
          "solid": "#1f5fa8",
          "on": "#f2f8ff",
          "text": "$blueDark",
          "edge": "$blueDark/26",
          "wash": "$blueDark/10"
        },
        "$comment_agent": "Entity identity — see the dark theme note. Darkened for AA on white.",
        "agent": {
          "solid": "#4c3475",
          "on": "#f7f2ff",
          "text": "$violetDark",
          "edge": "$violetDark/26",
          "wash": "$violetDark/10"
        }
      },
      "focus": { "ring": "$brassDark/26" },
      "scroll": {
        "thumb": "$scrollGreyLight/30",
        "thumbHover": "$scrollGreyLight/48",
        "track": "transparent"
      },
      "effects": {
        "$comment": "No panelSheen in light mode — an inner top highlight on a white card reads as a rendering bug. It is replaced by a real 1px shadow on elevCard. This is the ONLY structural fork between the two themes.",
        "panelSheen": null,
        "overlaySheen": {
          "type": "linearGradient",
          "angle": 180,
          "stops": [["#ffffff", "0%"], ["#f7f8fa", "100%"]]
        },
        "elevCard": {
          "type": "shadow",
          "layers": [
            { "inset": false, "x": 0, "y": 1, "blur": 2, "spread": 0, "color": "$shadowLight/6" }
          ]
        },
        "elevButton": {
          "type": "shadow",
          "layers": [
            { "inset": false, "x": 0, "y": 1, "blur": 2, "spread": 0, "color": "$shadowLight/8" }
          ]
        },
        "elevPopover": {
          "type": "shadow",
          "layers": [
            { "inset": false, "x": 0, "y": 14, "blur": 40, "spread": 0, "color": "$shadowLight/16" }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  },

  "scale": {
    "desktop": {
      "radius": { "sm": 6, "md": 8, "lg": 12, "xl": 14, "pill": 999 },
      "control": { "height": 34, "heightSm": 28, "borderWidth": 1, "iconGlyph": 17 },
      "scroll": { "width": 10, "inset": 3, "radius": 999 }
    },
    "mobile": {
      "$comment": "Radii are the desktop scale +2px: fingers read a 14px corner the way a cursor reads a 12px one. Control heights clear the 44pt iOS minimum, and app-bar glyphs are 24pt — at desktop's 17px they read as decoration instead of navigation.",
      "radius": { "sm": 8, "md": 10, "lg": 14, "xl": 18, "pill": 999 },
      "control": { "height": 44, "heightSm": 32, "borderWidth": 1, "iconGlyph": 24 },
      "scroll": { "width": 5, "inset": 0, "radius": 999 }
    }
  },

  "motion": {
    "$comment": "One easing curve for the whole system. Nothing bounces. Everything collapses to 0ms under prefers-reduced-motion / the mobile 'reduce motion' setting.",
    "enter": 140,
    "exit": 100,
    "easing": "cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.72, 0, 1)"
  }
}
